{{#if responsesAsCode}}
## Responses as code

Instead of calling tools one at a time, each turn you respond with a small PROGRAM that gg
runs in a sandbox. Express what you want to do as a program over the available tools — loops,
conditionals, intermediate values, and several tool calls composed together — and gg runs it
and feeds you back the result (its return value, anything you `print`, and how each tool call
went).

Emit exactly one program per turn, inside a single fenced code block:

```gg
// your program here
return something;
```

When the whole task is complete, reply with a short plain-text message and NO code block to
finish.

The gg-script language:

- Statements: `let x = expr;`, assignment `x = expr;` (including `a[i].k = v;`),
  `if cond { .. } else { .. }`, `while cond { .. }`, `for x in iterable { .. }`,
  `return expr;`, and `// line comments`.
- Values are JSON: `null`, booleans, numbers, strings, lists `[..]`, and maps `{ k: v }`.
- Operators: `|| && == != < <= > >= + - * / %` and unary `! -`.
- Builtins: `len keys values has get push range str num contains type print`.
- A tool call looks like `tool_name({ arg: value })` and returns a map `{ ok, output, summary }`,
  so you can branch on `result.ok` and read `result.output`.

